# Netlify — canonical URL enforcement.
#
# Every page is reachable at two URLs: /donate.html (the real file) and /donate
# (Netlify's clean URL). The canonical tag + sitemap declare the clean one, so
# Google reported the .html twins as "Alternate page with proper canonical tag"
# — crawled, understood, but never indexed. Internal links now point at the
# clean URLs; these 301s retire the .html twins for good (old links, bookmarks,
# and anything Google already has in its index).
#
# The `!` (force) is required: a real file exists at the source path, and
# without it Netlify would serve the file instead of redirecting.

/index.html     /          301!
/videos.html    /videos    301!
/gallery.html   /gallery   301!
/zmanim.html    /zmanim    301!
/donate.html    /donate    301!
/admin.html     /admin     301!
